        "original_id": "b4be19a9-4562-5b30-a6f9-07aa5757b184",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Albany International Airport; Dane County Regional Airport; Albany County, New York; Madison, Wisconsin\n- Codes: IATA ALB; ICAO KALB; FAA LID ALB; IATA MSN; ICAO KMSN; FAA LID MSN\n- Topics: airport location; airport type\n\nFacts:\n- Albany International Airport is a public airport located seven miles northwest of Albany in Albany County, New York, United States.\n- Albany International Airport uses the codes IATA ALB, ICAO KALB, and FAA LID ALB.\n- Dane County Regional Airport, also called Truax Field, is a civil-military airport located six miles northeast of downtown Madison, the capital of Wisconsin.\n- Dane County Regional Airport uses the codes IATA MSN, ICAO KMSN, and FAA LID MSN.",
